# Every text file checks out with LF, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# The tests read sources byte for byte. test/recipes.js compares the committed
# manifest exactly and holds each recipe under 6KB (the bytes the model is
# sent, \r included), and test/boot.js matches "\n        fireBuilt();\n" in
# viewer/index.html. A Windows checkout with autocrlf=true wrote CRLF and failed
# all three while the main copy, which happened to be LF, passed. The repo
# already stores everything as LF, so this changes no committed bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never converted, whatever the content sniffing would guess.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.wasm binary
*.stl binary
*.3mf binary
*.glb binary
*.zip binary
